      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Eq 8.5, upper scheme, alpha-i channel (arrow labelled 'ai'). McLafferty gamma-H rearrangement of the hexanal molecular ion (n-ionized at O, +. localized on oxygen exactly as drawn) with subsequent Ca-Cb cleavage; here the charge migrates to the C4H8 alkene (Stevenson competition, IE(butene)=9.6 eV printed left of the dashed line). The page draws 4 fishhook arcs shared by both 'or' outcomes (O-radical gamma-H abstraction; ring C=C formation; Ca-Cb cleavage). Moves 1-3 are drawn (H transfer); moves 4-5 encode the charge-retaining alkene ('i', inductive/heterolytic 2-electron cleavage of Ca-Cb with the oxocarbenium O=C pair collapsing to an O lone pair) and are NOT drawn as separate arcs. but-1-ene radical cation localized as the distonic form (+ on C4, odd e- on C5); the page draws the delocalized CH2=CH-CH2CH3 +. form. m/z is curator-computed; the 5% is printed. [RECHECK 2026-07-24: arc count corrected 3->4 per a zoomed re-read; the gamma-H abstraction is drawn as TWO barbs (O-radical->H and the gamma C-H bond electron->O-H), not one.]"
    },
    {
