        "section": null
      },
      "confidence": 0.4,
      "curator_note": "Cross-link: M\u00d8D rule IMS_8_5_1 (src/data_generation/rules/IMS_chap8_examples.py). Its skeleton matches this scheme (gamma-H -> O, Ca-Cb cleavage, Cb=Cg + enol C=C, charge on the C4H8 butene) BUT the rule is MIS-ENCODED: the carbonyl carbon is over-valent (valence 5, a spurious extra H -> reactant C6H13O not hexanal C6H12O) and its two product fragments each carry +1/1 radical (total +2 / 2 radicals) versus the +1/1 reactant, so it violates charge and spin conservation and would be dropped by the rules/__init__ conservation guardrail. Not RDKit-substructure-testable because the over-valent atoms are not a valid molecule."
